Sure! Below is a simple example of an “rotating card” that flips when you hover over it.  
It uses only **HTML** and **CSS** (no JavaScript).  

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* ---------- Container ----------
   Keeps the perspective so the flip looks 3‑D */
.card-wrapper {
    width: 300px;
    height: 200px;
    margin: 50px auto;
    perspective: 1000px;          /* depth of the 3‑D space */
}

/* ---------- Card ----------
   The element that actually rotates */
.card {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    position: relative;
    transform-style: preserve-3d;  /* allow children to be positioned in 3‑D space */
    transition: transform 0.6s ease; /* smooth animation */
    cursor: pointer;
}

/* ---------- Front & Back ----------
   Both sides occupy the same space, but we hide the back initially */
.front,
.back {
    position: absolute;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    backface-visibility: hidden;   /* hide the side facing away from the viewer */
    border-radius: 10px;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
}

.front {
    background: #fff;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: #333;
}

.back {
    background: #4a90e2;
    color: #fff;
    transform: rotateY(180deg);     /* start rotated so it's hidden */
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
}

/* ---------- Hover Effect ----------
   Flip the card when hovered */
.card:hover {
    transform: rotateY(180deg);
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <div class="front">Front Side</div>
        <div class="back">Back Side</div>
    </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Element | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `.card-wrapper` | Provides a 3‑D perspective (`perspective: 1000px`). |
| `.card` | The container that will rotate. `transform-style: preserve-3d` keeps its children in 3‑D space. |
| `.front`, `.back` | Two faces of the card. `backface-visibility: hidden` hides the side that’s turned away. |
| `.back` | Initially rotated 180° so it’s hidden. |
| `.card:hover` | Rotates the whole card 180°, revealing the back face. |

Feel free to replace the text or add images inside `.front` and `.back`. You can also tweak the dimensions, colors, or transition duration to fit your design. Enjoy!
